  33:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  34:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****    (#) For a given Stream, program the required configuration through the following parameters:
  35:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****        Transfer Direction, Source and Destination data formats, 
  36:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****        Circular, Normal or peripheral flow control mode, Stream Priority level, 
  37:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****        Source and Destination Increment mode, FIFO mode and its Threshold (if needed), 
  38:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****        Burst mode for Source and/or Destination (if needed) using HAL_DMA_Init() function.
  39:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  40:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****    -@-   Prior to HAL_DMA_Init() the clock must be enabled for DMA through the following macros:
  41:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****          __HAL_RCC_DMA1_CLK_ENABLE() or __HAL_RCC_DMA2_CLK_ENABLE().
  42:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  43:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****      *** Polling mode IO operation ***
  44:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****      =================================
  45:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****     [..]
  46:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Use HAL_DMA_Start() to start DMA transfer after the configuration of Source 
  47:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****               address and destination address and the Length of data to be transferred.
  48:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Use HAL_DMA_PollForTransfer() to poll for the end of current transfer, in this  
  49:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****               case a fixed Timeout can be configured by User depending from his application.
  50:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Use HAL_DMA_Abort() function to abort the current transfer.
  51:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  52:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****      *** Interrupt mode IO operation ***
  53:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****      ===================================
  54:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****     [..]
  55:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Configure the DMA interrupt priority using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority()
  56:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Enable the DMA IRQ handler using HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ() 
  57:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Use HAL_DMA_Start_IT() to start DMA transfer after the configuration of  
  58:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****               Source address and destination address and the Length of data to be transferred. In t
  59:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****               case the DMA interrupt is configured 
  60:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Use HAL_DMA_IRQHandler() called under DMA_IRQHandler() Interrupt subroutine
  61:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) At the end of data transfer HAL_DMA_IRQHandler() function is executed and user can 
  62:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****               add his own function by customization of function pointer XferCpltCallback and 
  63:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****               XferErrorCallback (i.e a member of DMA handle structure).
  64:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****     [..]
  65:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****      (#) Use HAL_DMA_GetState() function to return the DMA state and HAL_DMA_GetError() in case of 
  66:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****          detection.
  67:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  68:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****      (#) Use HAL_DMA_Abort_IT() function to abort the current transfer
  69:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  70:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****      -@-   In Memory-to-Memory transfer mode, Circular mode is not allowed.
  71:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  72:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****      -@-   The FIFO is used mainly to reduce bus usage and to allow data packing/unpacking: it is
  73:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****            possible to set different Data Sizes for the Peripheral and the Memory (ie. you can set
  74:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****            Half-Word data size for the peripheral to access its data register and set Word data siz
  75:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****            for the Memory to gain in access time. Each two half words will be packed and written in
  76:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****            a single access to a Word in the Memory).
  77:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c **** 
  78:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****      -@-   When FIFO is disabled, it is not allowed to configure different Data Sizes for Source
  79:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****            and Destination. In this case the Peripheral Data Size will be applied to both Source
  80:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c ****            and Destination.
  81:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_dma.c **** 
